			<div class="content" id="post-content-1434946">
									

<blockquote>
<p>SCP-1336 is a single sheet of 8 ½ X 11 inch 110&#160;lb cardstock</p>
</blockquote>
<p><em>All of the no</em>. We do not have 8.5&quot; x 11&quot; 110&#160;lb. cardstock at the Foundation.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>No opportunity to recover the paper came until several months after the Foundation learned of the existence of SCP-1336, when an explosion severely damaged the lab, killing 15 employees, including the informant. Foundation operatives were able to enter the lab and recover the object at that time.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>The Foundation has dozens, if not hundreds, of Mobile Task Forces at its disposal. Each is made up of the best and brightest soldiers the Foundation can find, many of them specially trained in close-quarters, urban combat, and they have essentially limitless funding and sway over local authorities. Why would we wait around and hope the facility blows up when we can just raid the place?</p>
<p>Aside from those points, and a few tone issues, it's actually an interesting idea.</p>

