														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1436331">
									

<p>While I appreciate that, you are crying over the wrong grave. This SCP is basically a paper with pictures of compounds that move about and &quot;react&quot;, if my tired head tells me right. Some of those symbols don't correspond to real elements. Which is OK because if depicting something, even by non-anomalous means required the thing to exist, there wouldn't be much art around.<br />
And I don't see where it says the foundation actually made them.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Of the 412 compounds that have yet to be synthesized, 53 appear to be physically impossible to synthesize using our current understanding of the nature of chemistry. Another 48 contain elements that do not appear on the periodic table. (Element Za appears in 15 of these molecules.)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>In other words, the Foundation hasn't synthetised them yet, and noone suggests they might.</p>

