														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1437524">
									

<p>Um, that's the thing with this SCP.<br />
It <em>displays</em> a bunch of elements and reactions associated with them, evidently using rules that in some ways are like our chemistry and in some aren't.</p>
<p>For all we know, the compounds are indeed implausible and might not be real. Or they work in an universe with subtly different physics, and the thingy was misprogrammed. Who knows.</p>
<p>My point is that this SCP is the type of usage of non-existant elements that <strong>doesn't</strong> scream physicsfail , as it never asserts such exist. In fact the absurdity of them is what makes the thing interesting.</p>

							</div>

								
