														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1453724">
									

<p>I fixed the chemical jargon. (Genesplicer, aren't you a high school chemistry teacher? You should know better!)</p>
<p>It's not that they have elements that are not on the periodic table. It's that the formulas contain symbols that are <em>not known to represent elements or functional groups</em>.</p>
<p>And don't say that the chemicals are &quot;impossible to synthesize&quot;. Just because we don't know how to synthesize a given molecule doesn't mean it's anomalous. The point is that the molecules should be impossible <em>according to currently-accepted theories of chemical bonding</em>.</p>

							</div>

								
					
