			<div class="content" id="post-content-1453897">
									

<p>Well, no, not high school. 8th grade. It's a bit more simplified (and sometimes the oversimplification leads to errors. For example, we don't discuss electron orbitals, we simply state that electrons orbit in specific patterns around the nucleus. I explain to my students that I am oversimplifying, but the reality is probably beyond their grasp until they've had a few more math classes.) Since I wrote this one during our Chem unit, I ended up using an oversimplified language. I'll have to watch that.</p>

